4. SUPER+SHIFT+ALT+B (browser private): default \"SUPER + SHIFT + ALT + B\" → stays. Collision → unbind first.\n5. ALT+RETURN (Terminal): default \"SUPER + RETURN\" → swapped → \"ALT + RETURN\" (Terminal). Collision → unbind first.\n6. SUPER+ALT+RETURN (Tmux): default \"SUPER + ALT + RETURN\" → stays (tmux). Collision → unbind first.\n7. ALT+SHIFT+RETURN (Browser): default \"SUPER + SHIFT + RETURN\" → swapped \"ALT + SHIFT + RETURN\". Collision → unbind first.\n8. ALT+SHIFT+O (OCR): no default on that. But we removed OCR from ALT+CTRL+PRINT.\n9. SUPER+SPACE (launch-app): default \"SUPER + SPACE\" → swapped → \"ALT + SPACE\". Wait! The wrapper swaps SUPER+SPACE → ALT+SPACE. The override wanted ALT+SPACE = launch walker. User bindings.conf: SUPER+SPACE = launch-app. So after wrapper: ALT+SPACE = omarchy-menu toggle (swapped default). Then in bindings.lua:\n   - unbind \"ALT + SPACE\" (the swapped omarchy menu)... hmm wait, but the user's override said `unbind = SUPER, SPACE; bindd = ALT, SPACE, Launch apps, exec, omarchy-launch-walker`. The old default SUPER+SPACE was omarchy menu? Old: SUPER+SPACE = launch walker probably. Under user's scheme: ALT+SPACE = omarchy-launch-walker, SUPER+SPACE = launch-app.\n   - The default \"SUPER + ALT + SPACE\" (Apps menu) stays.\n   - Post-default: unbind \"ALT + SPACE\" (swapped omarchy menu), bind \"ALT + SPACE\" → \"omarchy-launch-walker\", bind \"SUPER + SPACE\" → \"launch-app\". ✓\n   \n10. SUPER+D wayscriber: default \"SUPER + CTRL + D\" (Display panel) → swapped \"ALT + CTRL + D\"; \"SUPER + SHIFT + D\" (Docker) → \"ALT + SHIFT + D\". Plain SUPER+D free. ✓\n11. SUPER+mouse_down/up zoom: after wrapper, SUPER+mouse_down no longer exists (moved to ALT+mouse_down). Bind SUPER+mouse_down → zoom. ✓\n12. ALT+SHIFT+O OCR: free. Also need unbind \"ALT + CTRL + PRINT\" (swapped OCR) since user removed it from there.\n\nNow, the tmux: user's is SUPER+ALT+RETURN with custom exec. Default is SUPER+ALT+RETURN with omarchy terminal-tmux hel