lt = true (same as default)\n- touchpad: natural_scroll = true (default is false!), clickfinger_behavior = true (same), scroll_factor = 0.4 (same)\n- windowrule scroll_touchpad for Alacritty|kitty|foot 1.5, ghostty 0.2 (same as default — o.window)\n- gestures: 3 left/right movefocus, 2 pinch cursorZoom — the default only had commented gestures. User's conf has:\n  ```\n  gesture = 3, left,  dispatcher, movefocus, l\n  gesture = 3, right, dispatcher, movefocus, r\n  gesture = 2, pinch, cursorZoom, 2\n  ```\n  Port to hl.gesture:\n  ```lua\n  hl.gesture({ fingers = 3, direction = \"left\", action = function() hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.focus({ direction = \"l\" })) end })\n  hl.gesture({ fingers = 3, direction = \"right\", action = function() hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.focus({ direction = \"r\" })) end })\n  hl.gesture({ fingers = 2, direction = \"pinch\", action = \"cursorZoom\", zoom_level = 2 })\n  ```\n  The template comment shows the focus pattern: `hl.gesture({ fingers = 3, direction = \"left\", action = function() hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.focus({ direction = \"l\" })) end })`. ✓ For cursorZoom: old conf `gesture = 2, pinch, cursorZoom, 2` — args \"cursorZoom\", 2 (zoom level). Lua: `hl.gesture({ fingers = 2, direction = \"pinch\", action = \"cursorZoom\", zoom_level = 2 })`? The comment in input.conf says: \"Equivalent of hl.gesture({fingers=2, direction=\"pinch\", action=\"cursorZoom\", zoom_level=2})\". So use that exact form. ✓\n\nSince input.lua runs after defaults (which already set things), I should only override what differs. To be explicit and faithful, I'll set the full input config with the user's values (kb_options differs, natural_scroll differs, plus repeat_rate etc. redundant but harmless).\n\nNote: default input.lua reads vconsole for layout — user hardcoded \"us\". Port \"us\".\n\nNow hyprland.lua in dotfiles: template + wrapper.\n\nWait, actually — do I even need the wrapper to live in hyprland.lua? Yes, must be before require(\"default.hypr.omarchy\").\n\nNow, one 