        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Done. Your previous config is now live under omarchy quattro, symlinked from your dotfiles repo:\n\n**Files created in `~/dev/environment/home/.config/hypr/` and symlinked into `~/.config/hypr/`:**\n- `hyprland.lua` — restores the full **SUPER→ALT swap**: a wrapper installed only while Omarchy defaults load rebinds every default SUPER binding (without ALT) to ALT, so it survives future omarchy updates. Your own SUPER bindings stay SUPER.\n- `input.lua` — port of `input.conf`: `us` layout, `compose:caps,ctrl:nocaps`, natural scroll, 3-finger focus gestures, 2-finger pinch zoom.\n- `bindings.lua` — port of `bindings.conf` + `bindings-override.conf`: terminal/browser/file-manager on ALT, OCR on `ALT+SHIFT+O`, screenshot trio (SUPER+PRINT record / ALT+PRINT picker), SUPER+mouse zoom, wayscriber, TAB/monitor group swaps, precise volume/brightness on SUPER, `ALT+XF86AudioMute` output switch, CTRL+SUPER+DELETE close-all.\n\n**Notes:**\n- Dead commands were mapped to modern equivalents: `launch-app`/`omarchy-launch-walker` → `omarchy-menu toggle apps`, `omarchy-capture-text-extraction` → `omarchy-capture-text`, screenrecord → `omarchy-capture-screenrecording`. The old `code:61` scaling-cycle binding was dropped (command gone; `ALT+SLASH` scales now).\n- The old `.conf` symlinks stay in place (harmless reference); stock `.lua` templates were backed up as `*.omarchy-stock.bak.*`.\n- Validated with `hyprctl reload` — zero config errors; spot-checked 60+ bindings, all swapped correctly.",
